# mcp__mcp_agent_mail_fetch_inbox — mcp-agent-mail/fetch_inbox

Retrieve recent messages for an agent and mark returned messages read.

Filters
-------
- `urgent_only`: only messages with importance in {high, urgent}
- `unread_only`: only recipient rows whose read_ts is unset
- `ack_overdue_only`: only ack-required rows with no ack_ts older than the 30-minute SLA
- `since_ts`: ISO-8601 timestamp string; messages strictly newer than this are returned
- `limit`: max number of messages (default 20)
- `include_bodies`: include full Markdown bodies in the payloads
- `topic`: exact case-insensitive topic filter

Usage patterns
--------------
- Poll after each editing step in an agent loop to pick up coordination messages.
- Use `since_ts` with the timestamp from your last poll for efficient incremental fetches.
- Combine with `acknowledge_message` if `ack_required` is true.

Returns
-------
list[dict]
    Each message includes: { id, subject, topic?, from, created_ts, read_ts?, ack_ts?, importance, ack_required, kind, [body_md] }

Example
-------
```json
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":"7","method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"fetch_inbox","arguments":{
  "project_key":"/abs/path/backend","agent_name":"BlueLake","since_ts":"2025-10-23T00:00:00+00:00"
}}}
```

mark_read : Optional[bool]
    Default true. Set false for a non-consuming peek that never changes read state (used by `am check-inbox` and other monitoring hooks).

## Schema
```ts
type Args = {
  topic?: string | null;
  since_ts?: string | null;
  ack_overdue_only?: boolean | null;
  mark_read?: boolean | null;
  urgent_only?: boolean | null;
  include_bodies?: boolean | null;
  unread_only?: boolean | null;
  project_key: string;
  agent_name: string;
  limit?: number | null;
};
```
Execute by writing JSON to xd://mcp__mcp_agent_mail_fetch_inbox.

